    "message": "Reuse the archive key of a list chunk saved before by the same writer\n\nEvery save rebuilt the bytes of each list chunk (about 300 for a day's\nEventLog), hashed them and checked the chunk file, although most chunks\nheld history saved before. The history cache reuses the item bytes of\nthat history, so a chunk with the same first and last item objects and\nlength holds the same bytes; its key is remembered per writer and reused\nwhile its file exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
